WEBVTT

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.460
The story until now.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:16.340
In flowery Tokyo lived Nozomu, a spirit medium popular for some reason among the middle-aged.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:22.700
He was invited to the faraway village Moushiwake-Arima-Son, where all greetings, from “hello” to “good night”,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.000
were given prostrated.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.450
The chief of the village, the name of which means “35-year-old NEET” in Sanskrit, said:

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.260
“Something terrible has happened to the maidens of our village.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.590
They have read, and fallen under the curse of, proletarian literature.”

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:42.910
and led him to the inner parlor, where he encountered that which the villagers feared as a once-in-a-century ill omen:

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.020
reverse prostration.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.410
It was not that a forward-facing prostration was impossible, but there,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.920
as a statement that he must as a spirit medium open the wrapping paper, he said:

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.030
“This is Kemco's CG.”

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.430
Drink plenty of Calmotine, and it'll go away.

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.110
The seniors are having their graduation ceremony.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:49.280
Back-scratch-

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:49.450
-arat

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:49.610
cards

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:49.780
on

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:49.950
sale

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:50.210
soon

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.550
What are you getting all twitchy about?

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.120
I'm not getting twitchy about anything!

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.860
It's not like I'm afraid to go congratulate them or anything!

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.330
You're afraid.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.100
I said I wasn't!

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.100
Hey, Despair!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.110
Are you some kind of middle-school girl, walking around with that thing!?

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.510
Teacher, you're not in charge of the seniors, so it shouldn't matter to you.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.350
More importantly, what's this?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.550
A tearful graduation ceremony?

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.590
Graduations really are things to cry at,

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.890
but if it's written out like this I can't cry anymore.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:37.500
It seems you understand well.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.130
Japanese can no longer be overenthusiastic about catch copy like this.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.940
We're still watching.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.070
Still watching.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:54.310
I can't laugh at things called “hilarious” anymore.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:58.750
That kind of introduction just makes us skeptical.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:03.490
Things which bill themselves as moving finales have become unable to move us!

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:07.830
By calling normal citizens pros, we can no longer interact with our neighbors!

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:12.460
By calling our nation paradise on earth, it feels like it absolutely can't be paradise!

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:15.330
If I have to pick a name for it, it's back-scratching! {hurf this is the best I can do; he's punning "overdoing it" with "shoulder rubs"}

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.900
Is probably the best way to put it.

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.270
When I was in middle school,

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:24.280
they said that I was an interesting person!

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:28.710
See? No matter what she says, it won't be interesting.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.650
Really.

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.620
These are all flashes in the pan caused by media propaganda!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.250
Scratch something's back too much and it becomes unbelievable!

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.560
By being overpromoted,

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.390
things just get dragged down!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.640
Stop it!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.200
Seriously, stop it!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.410
Aww, come on.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:59.180
If you can't carry at least this burden, you won't have a fighting chance!

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:00.710
Won't have a fighting chance?

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.850
Over here.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:13.420
Somehow, we've wandered into a world where everything has its back scratched.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.660
You were there?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.260
Yes, always.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.500
Behold.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.730
Over there is a restaurant that's had its back scratched.

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.700
Well, you do see restaurants like this.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.340
A restaurant with plenty of back-scratching...

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.210
They're kind of redundant.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.310
We've been waiting for you.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.420
It's had its back scratched plenty, so there should be no problem, brother.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.450
What are you trying to start, Rin?

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:42.690
A game of cards.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.220
Backscratcharat.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.860
Backscratcharat?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.500
The rules are just like Old Maid. {this is kumeta's fuckup, not mine}

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:56.600
Everyone but the first player to win has to bear the bac-scratching on the cards they haven't discarded.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.200
Why don't we give it a try? Then you'll understand.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.240
Wow, these are really—

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.180
Super Zetsubou-sensei.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.910
Alluring Zetsubou-sensei.

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:09.250
Showa King of Laughing Zetsubou-sensei.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.920
They suck! They all suck! I wanna discard!

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.490
This one sucks too!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.590
This kind of backscratching is the kind of thing that'll get you arrested! {note}

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.270
You're drawing some pretty horrible cards for yourself, too.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:31.940
Asian Beauty Normal.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.170
Alluring Normal.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.770
Normal of Love and Youth.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.210
Super Normal.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.510
Come on! I'm not named “Normal”!

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.310
Uno!

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.980
This time I really need an inoffensive card...

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.460
This sucks! This backscratching sucks!

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.600
Hyper Media Creator Zetsubou.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.900
Bro, you're so cool!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.840
It's nothing to laugh about, Rin!

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:09.510
If I don't get rid of this card quick...

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.080
Take it! Hurry up and take that card!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:17.180
By the way, there are also tense games taking place at the other tables.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.790
This backscratching sucks! I've gotta get rid of it soon!

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.870
If I don't discard it soon—!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:40.470
I'm ending up with more and more backscratching that I can't bear!

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:43.270
These are the kinds of things a middle-schooler would doodle a comic about!

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.250
I'm done!

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.530
Mr. Big Bang!

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:09.370
When he's around, you know something will happen.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.940
Why?

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:14.070
Because he's Mr. Big Bang!

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:18.040
Next week the Big Bang will happen.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.710
No, it'll just be like normal.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:24.950
I've heard of Mr. “Big Magnum” Kuroiwa, but...

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:38.100
I can't brighten up.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:43.500
All this year, my heart's been clouded.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:46.070
I'm blue.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:50.780
Why?

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.280
Because of leaps. {this is it. this is the untranslatable part. I'm so glad it's coming on a week when the guy from Suimasen has swine flu.}

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:57.580
There was a leap second this year on January 1st.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.780
It's been irritating me since then!

00:08:59.780 --> 00:08:59.950
Thanks

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:00.120
for buying

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:00.280
the opening single

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:00.450
Apple

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:00.620
Picking

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:00.890
Beam

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:11.800
This year, on January 1st at 9AM, a leap second was added.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.970
Why was that second created?

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.240
Why couldn't they keep it nice and neat!?

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:19.970
It's just a second, it doesn't matter.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.140
If they didn't mention it, no one would even notice.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:24.880
No one would even notice?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.350
What's wrong, teacher?

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.650
A leap second is just fine.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.850
Compared to how this class may be filling up with leap people!

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:39.160
Leap...

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:39.960
...people?

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:44.800
There's leap years and leap seconds, so what's wrong with leap people!?

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.300
They come in without you even knowing it.

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:51.670
Wouldn't the class realize if there was an extra person?

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:53.670
Would they? Really?

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:59.840
Were days or hours to increase or disappear, without clocks and calendars,

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.180
just how many people do you think would notice?

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.190
But everyone knows in advance!

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:09.350
Do they really?

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:13.790
Leap seconds exist in a careless, spontaneous pattern.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:19.860
Leap people may well exist spontaneously as if they've been there the whole time!

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:26.100
Well, I get that you're trying to say something philosophical.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.870
There may be a leap person among us!

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:40.120
Well, in life there are plenty of times when there's one person too many.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.620
When flights are overbooked.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:47.030
When an editor from Magazine shows up uninvited at a mixer for Afternoon.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:50.030
When an amateur decides to show up for ADR.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:54.530
It's extremely likely that those phenomena are the work of leap people!

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.140
Teacher.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.070
Oh no, teacher!

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.340
You were there?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.510
Yes, always.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:05.510
It appears that leap people infest even shopping arcades.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.480
Are you okay?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.880
Th—the number of people increased!

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:17.620
There were 40 packs, one per customer,

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:20.390
but they were taken up by only 39 people!

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:21.990
Wow, that's scary!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.900
It must have been the work of the leap people!

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.500
Didn't someone just come through the line twice?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.170
I saw one!

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:33.000
A leap person was in the elevator!

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.610
In the elevator with an occupancy limit of 5!

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.120
There were only five people riding, but the overweight buzzer went off!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.350
There had to be a leap person on board!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.220
Well, ummm, that's...

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.020
Leap people can occur in groups, too!

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:58.700
And they carry out a vital role in Japan's economy! {jesus fuck she looks :downs: here shaft are you ragequitting like you did for bake}

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.170
Just yesterday...

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:08.640
Today's attendance is 55,000.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.980
50,000, with that many empty seats!?

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.810
Obviously, leap people came to watch.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.450
Er...

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:22.020
For CDs that no one buys to top the Oricon charts,

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:25.460
masses of leap people must be buying them!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.190
No, that's—

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:31.200
For the organizers to claim 110,000 when only 2000 people showed up,

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:34.930
108,000 leap people must have participated!

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:39.540
Leap people support Japan from the shadows!

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.810
Leap seconds irritate me enough.

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.010
Now there's leap people?

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:45.410
And in groups?

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.510
I'll cut them back down to the proper number!

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:48.410
Hold it!

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.150
Chiri, you might be a leap person!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.050
Me!?

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.820
That's stupid!

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.290
Try to remember, Chiri! {or "i remember", pick one}

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:03.290
Happy birthday to you!

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:08.600
Oh my, you only invited five, but one more of your friends showed up.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.740
A girl I didn't invite came.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:12.840
A girl I didn't invite came.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.070
A girl I didn't invite came. {young Harumi sure loved her KFC.}

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.240
Coming along on a friend's date.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.450
Going along with a friend to the salon, and not getting a trim, just waiting and reading comics.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:25.080
We can suspect you of being a leap person!

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.450
No way!

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:32.720
Cake sliced a little too thin

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:36.860
Because someone extra showed up

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:45.740
Reducing the number of mouths to feed is a sin

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:49.010
Stone chirashi-zushi

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.780
Then won't you join our group?

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.280
Who are you?

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:57.380
We're the Leap Man Group. {again}

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:02.420
Just what is this?

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.060
Don't you know?

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:08.860
It's the Leap Man Group, popular among subculture-loving coeds.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.300
Look, more members are coming out.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:16.400
A baseball player's second wife. A leap wife!

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:20.670
The leap members of an idol group that grew too big!

00:14:20.970 --> 00:14:24.910
A leap superstar who's in Milan now for some reason!

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:30.650
And it's not just limited to people and time; there's leap everything!

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.750
Even the secondhand goods that they use!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:38.260
Leap magazines that get overprinted even though magazines don't sell anymore!

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:43.430
Things that you can't imagine coming out on Bluray are Leap-Ray Discs!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:48.430
Leap menus, posted in cafes even though you can't order from them!

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.940
Leap things are everywhere!

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:54.470
And here comes their specialty!

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:56.670
A physical performance!

00:14:56.670 --> 00:15:01.050
A long hair that grew somewhere weird; a leap hair!

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:05.280
A third eye that appears after much training; a leap eye!

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:08.520
Using an audience member!?

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:12.060
They put Hito on stage!

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:15.030
What kind of leap thing does she have?

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.030
Leap guts.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.300
Leap guts?

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.530
I don't have that kind of excess internal organ!

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:32.280
It's her appendix.

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:36.010
Well, you can't say you don't have leap guts.

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:37.520
How normal.

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:39.750
Don't call me normal.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:45.720
Today's attendance was 52,000.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:49.090
Now that I think about it, there's no way there could be leap people.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.230
They're just padding the numbers.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.710
We'd planned on five girls, but six came!

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.880
A leap gal is fine too. {yes, this is the author of Hayate}

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:43.550
Anyway, I keep picturing all these little kids playing some game in this big field of rye and all.

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:43.720
Thousands of little kids, and nobody's around - nobody big, I mean - except me.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:43.880
And I'm standing on the edge of some crazy cliff.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:44.050
What I have to do, I have 
to catch everybody if they 
start to go over the cliff 
- I mean if they're running 
and they don't look where 
they're going I have to 
come out from somewhere 
and catch them.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:44.220
That's all I do all day. I'd just be the catcher in the rye and all.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:44.480
I know it's crazy, but that's the only thing I'd really like to be.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:01.470
Yes, you certainly have caught me.

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:04.440
But how about catch and release?

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.900
Catch and release?

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:07.810
Why?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.040
Because, after all, today

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.840
-is- Houjoue.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:14.610
Houjoue?

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:16.950
It's a Buddhist holiday.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:21.290
A day where you do good deeds like letting go the fish or animals you catch.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:25.990
Also, you overlook the failings and mistakes of others.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.390
So today, I'd like you to release me,

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:32.900
and also to overlook what happened with my body double last week!

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:35.630
Thank you for releasing me!

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:44.180
What's up with your sudden appearance?

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:48.250
The kindness to let something go through one ear and out the other. {yes i know it's in one eal but having "through" to pun on is vital}

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.620
Houjoue isn't just a day, perhaps it's also the lifestyle of Japanese people.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.220
That being “through life”.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.850
Through... life?

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:00.430
I've heard of “slow life”, but...

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.760
No, “through life”.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.460
Ignoring people passed out in the street!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:07.270
Ignoring the cries of the neighbors' kids!

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:10.500
Ignoring cruel bullying in the classroom!

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:13.540
The ability to overlook those is the kindness of the Japanese!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.570
Well, um...

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:19.610
That isn't quite... wait, why am I in all the examples?

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:23.380
Teacher, you've recently decided to try out "through life", haven't you.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:24.720
No, I haven't!

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:28.720
This is the Rohas family. They're trying "through life", too.

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:30.590
Hi, we're the Rohases.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.420
What?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.390
Oh, nothing.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:37.200
"Through life", teacher.

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:41.800
The wife is pretty, too.

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:46.240
"Through life", teacher.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.640
This is my daughter, Sokotoko.

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:52.840
Through life, through life.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:55.910
Here, why not have lunch?

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:01.090
I'm terribly sorry, but where is this eel from?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:03.690
Since it's through food...

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.720
Through... food?

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:10.760
Eel is slow food, but if you don't know where it came from it's through food too.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:15.470
Letting safety, provenance, and toxicity go through one ear and out the other;

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.470
that's through food.

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:24.940
I feel there's quite a societal difference between slow food and through food.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.550
This is the supermarket we usually go to.

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.480
It has a great variety of through food.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:35.920
Processed foods where you ignore what meat is used.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.090
Dairy products where you ignore their reuse.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.690
Brand-name rice that's obviously too cheap.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:42.760
Come on, you shouldn't ignore those!

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:44.000
Hey,

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.930
what's up with these veggies!

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:48.270
Why don't you neatly display where they came from!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.240
Oh, teacher.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:56.570
Through life?

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:59.710
It's a kind lifestyle where you ignore many things.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:04.080
Didn't we use this same kind of gag a long time ago?

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.850
Ignore that too.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:09.350
Teacher, it looks like you finally get through life!

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.460
You mean like what we just did?

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:16.390
It's not that bad. I think I'll try it out.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:21.200
Ignoring that.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:26.700
Definitely ignoring that.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:28.570
Ignoring that.

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:29.540
Ignoring that.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.380
Ignoring that.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.180
Ignoring that.

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:31.940
Ignoring that.

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:33.680
I'm ignoring them all!

00:20:35.780 --> 00:20:39.650
If you put it that way, I'm experiencing through life too.

00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:40.750
Ohkusa?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.060
Even though I know it, I ignore when my husband's horny.

00:20:46.060 --> 00:20:50.360
I don't have the money to go to hospital, so I ignore pains.

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:54.470
I ignore N-bleep-K's demands for money.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:57.340
If I don't ignore them, I wouldn't be able to go on with my daily life!

00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:01.840
I don't know how to put this, but I'm sorry for ignoring things as a hobby.

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:44.640
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:54.890
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:02.960
Lightning...

00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:04.600
Flash!

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:10.970
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:14.170
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.170 --> 00:23:16.940
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.180 --> 00:23:20.580
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:24.920
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:28.650
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.650 --> 00:23:31.520
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:33.890
Bye bye!
